Case Study of AR-HUD Interface
Once the visual index z of the AR-HUD is computed, the interface is partitioned into six sections using an 800x600 resolution. By defining the radius r and adopting a basic unit length of 1.57mm, a fundamental unit grid is established. Taking into account the intensity of visual perception, the model is further divided into six modules, and the significance of each basic HUD module unit was ascertained using a priority-based approach.
